        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2e26a11b-cfa8-5728-a91c-0b377b4629ed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carlton House, Carlton House Terrace, London\n- People: George IV, George III\n- Roles: Prince Regent, King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, King of Hanover\n- Organizations: Crown Estate\n\nFacts:\n- George IV was born as George Augustus Frederick on 12 August 1762.\n- Carlton House was a mansion in London and became the town residence of the Prince Regent from 1783 for several decades.\n- From 1811 until his accession, George IV served as Prince Regent during the final mental illness of his father, George III.\n- George IV became King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland and of Hanover after George III died on 29 January 1820.\n- George IV died on 26 June 1830.\n- Carlton House Terrace was built on the site of Carlton House.\n- The freehold of Carlton House Terrace still belongs to the Crown Estate.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a0faaea3-45cb-5e22-b8f7-59dc0851513c",
        "text": "Page: Carlton House. Sentence: Carlton House was a mansion in London, best known as the town residence of the Prince Regent for several decades from 1783.\nPage: George IV of the United Kingdom. Sentence: George IV (George Augustus Frederick; 12 August 1762 – 26 June 1830) was King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland and of Hanover following the death of his father, George III, on 29 January 1820, until his own death ten years later.\nPage: George IV of the United Kingdom. Sentence: From 1811 until his accession, he served as Prince Regent during his father's final mental illness.\nPage: Carlton House Terrace. Sentence: They took the place of Carlton House, and the freehold still belongs to the Crown Estate.",
